A.practical=dict(graph='Plot reflected angle vertically against incident angle horizontally; both are measured from the normal.',unit='degree/degree, dimensionless',meaning='The gradient is the ratio of reflection-angle change to incidence-angle change. A slope near one with near-zero intercept supports r = i.',method=['Place a plane mirror along a marked line on paper and mark an incidence point.','Draw a normal perpendicular to the mirror line.','Direct a narrow ray-box beam to the point and mark incident and reflected paths using separated points.','Remove the apparatus and use a protractor to measure both angles from the normal.','Repeat across several angles and repeat alignments to assess reading variation.'],control='Keep the mirror upright and on its line, use thin marks, avoid parallax and do not direct a beam into eyes.',table='Record incidence angle / degree and reflection angle / degree for each trial.',conclusion='Compare fitted slope with one and intercept with zero, allowing for angle-reading uncertainty; systematic offset may indicate a misplaced normal.')
